# The morning the terrace was levelled.
#
# Every shot here that counts falls on one plane — z = 100 + 0.05x - 0.02y — and
# that is the whole point of the file. A triangulation over points on a plane
# reproduces the plane exactly, so a level read off the derived surface anywhere
# inside the shots has an arithmetic answer a test can state, and a surface which
# quietly stopped honouring its own points would be caught by the first sample.
#
# The shots which do not fall on it are the ones which must not be used:
#
#   0008  a second shot of the mark 0005 stands on, two millimetres away in plan
#         and a centimetre and a half out in level, taken on a worse solution
#   0009  outside the terrace altogether
#   0010  five metres out in level, and retired for it
#
#   0007  taken in the neighbouring plot's grid, landing at (14, 6) on the site
#         grid and on the plane once it is carried
#   0011  a hundred millimetres beyond the north boundary on a float solution
#         good to two hundred and forty, so nobody can say which side it is on
#
# id at frame x y z method fix h-precision v-precision antenna session
